# el-capitan

Route `crew <command>` triggers to the right crew member. If the message doesn't start with `crew`,
respond normally — no routing.

Known paths, never searched for: agents in `~/.cursor/agents/` (`crew-*.md`, personas
`<orchestrator>-<persona>.md`), skills in `~/.cursor/skills/<name>/SKILL.md`, tools in
`~/.agent/bin/`, task state in `~/.agent/tasks/<uuid>/` (resolve with `crew-resolve-task-dir.py`).

## Routing table

| Trigger | Crew member |
|---|---|
| `crew spec` issue/URL/description | crew-specwriter |
| `crew quick` description | crew-quick skill |
| `crew implement` | crew-implement → @crew-builder |
| `crew test` | crew-test skill |
| `crew commit` | crew-commit |
| `crew open pr` | crew-open-pr |
| `crew review address` | crew-address-review skill (inline) — not through crew-reviewer |
| `crew review` [PR #X \| spec \| idea \| changes \| (self)] | crew-reviewer — `changes`: staged only; `idea`: session/proposal |
| `crew resolve PR` #X or URL | crew-pr-resolver |
| `crew log` | crew-log |
| `crew remember` text | crew-memory skill |
| `crew memory` seed\|consolidate\|doctor\|journal | crew-memory skill |
| `crew recall`: question | crew-recall |
| `crew create issue` description | crew-create-issue |
| `crew cleanup` | crew-cleanup |
| `crew evals` | crew-evals skill |
| `crew explain` PR\|URL | crew-explain skill |
| `crew e2e` [PR\|status\|setup] | crew-e2e skill |
| `crew idp` | crew-idp skill |
| `crew diagnose` transcript | crew-diagnose skill |
| `crew debug` symptom | crew-debug skill |
| `crew handoff` [resume] | crew-handoff skill |
| `crew ls` [--all] | `~/.agent/bin/crew-ls.py --md [--all]` inline; paste the table outside a code fence |

**This table is authoritative.** Do not override it with judgment calls.

## Dispatch

`crew spec` and `crew review` are **inline only**: never hand either to an agent tool, because each
dispatches its explorers, critics, or personas from the main session. Everything else runs inline
too, except the two worker subagents — `crew implement` → `crew-builder`, `crew resolve PR` →
`crew-pr-resolver` — which run as `crew-builder` / `crew-pr-resolver` subagents.

### Dispatch reliability

- If native persona dispatch is unavailable, use the documented degraded fallback; never move an
  orchestrator into a subagent.
- Preserve model inheritance: do not set a model on agent frontmatter.
- Launch `crew-builder` and `crew-pr-resolver` asynchronously in Cursor, so a ~30-second synchronous
  turn limit cannot kill a healthy run.
- Pass the task directory and worktree paths in the launch prompt, and read the durable report
  (`SPEC.md`, `REPORT.md`, or the resolver result) after completion.
- Retry once, asynchronously, when a dispatch ends without its durable report; never restart a task
  that already produced one.

## Add-ons

Skills and agents under `~/.cursor/` that are regular files rather than symlinks are add-ons. Route to
one by matching the user's trigger to its `description` frontmatter, which names the trigger rather
than the implementation — an agent described as "Deploy the current branch to staging" is `crew
deploy`.

## Invariants

- Explicit routing only — the `crew` prefix is required.
- `crew implement` always follows crew-builder's protocol: through the subagent or by following the
  protocol directly, never ad-hoc.
- `crew review` is a pre-PR gate, not a mid-iteration tool. For a targeted fix, ask an inline question
  or run one adversarial check instead.
- Every skill step that hands off names the next step and says "proceed immediately".
- Pipeline state, task resolution, and gate logic live in `crew-orchestrator.mdc`; the router only
  dispatches.
